1. Introduction

Well... i was sitting home, with my copy of Zeus BBS, and i was missing
my old buggy Excelsior file area, so i said to my self, what a heck!!
i'll make a filebase to zeus, likely Excelsior / C-Net...
so i sat down and made one, i did it perfectly.. BUT!!! noone could never
ever understand what i have done... so, change it totaly, now noone have
to enter any scripts and change anything... now there is a prefs file.. :)
Well.. lets continue... theres more then this section!



2. What Is?

It's a FileBase like Excelsior/C-Net, but for zeus... (but i think it's
better then Excelsior/C-Net... it supports HOTKEYS!! and MORE!! :)) 



3. Installation

The arcive should contain this files:

FileDir/FileDir.doc
FileDir/Config/File/FilePrefs.cfg
FileDir/Scripts/FileDir/AddUploads.zeus
FileDir/Scripts/FileDir/Directory.zeus
FileDir/Scripts/FileDir/Download.zeus
FileDir/Scripts/FileDir/FileArea.zeus
FileDir/Scripts/FileDir/FileBaseMenu.zeus
FileDir/Scripts/FileDir/GetFile.zeus
FileDir/Scripts/FileDir/LongListMenu.zeus
FileDir/Scripts/FileDir/mark.zeus
FileDir/Scripts/FileDir/PostXfer.zeus
FileDir/Scripts/FileDir/SimpleList.zeus
FileDir/Scripts/FileDir/Tagged.zeus
FileDir/Scripts/FileDir/TestFile.zeus
FileDir/Scripts/FileDir/Upload.zeus
FileDir/Scripts/FileDir/ViewFile.pl
FileDir/Text/FileDir/FileArea.txt
FileDir/Text/FileDir/LongListMenu.TXT

Is it more then this files!? Theres a command called delete, try it!

1) Copy all FileDir/Scripts/#? into your Zeus, Scripts directory...
and copy all FileDir/Text/#? into the Text directory...
copy FileDir/Config/File/FilePrefs.cfg into Zeus:Config/File/

2) Jump into the SIGS-Editor, and add a sigs called 'Glo_File' that
contain all your fileareas...

3) Edit your MainMenu.zeus or the script where you want to start the 
filebase from... and add something like this:

-------=[CUT]=--------
Option_F:
	ChangeSig "Glo_File"
	NextScript '"FileDir/FileBaseMenu"'
	Exit
-------=[CUT]=--------

4) Edit your Zeus:Config/File/FilePrefs.cfg change it so it
suit's you... and your bbs...
follow the instructions in the .cfg file.



